# Egyptian Lime Mortar Curing Simulation
# TRIG6 Model: Lime mortar/concrete (CaO + sand + water → Ca(OH)2 → CaCO3)
# θ = curing phase, R = bond strength, D = shrinkage drift, N = aggregate noise
# Danger: quicklime heat tan∞ (burns/weak bond)

# Initial configuration - balanced curing
set eq 1.0
theta pi/4  # Balanced cure phase (45 degrees)
alpha 0.3
theta_opt pi/6  # Optimal strength phase (30 degrees)

# Step 1: Initial hydration state
step
state  # Expected: R=0.8 (strength), D=0.2 (crack), N=0.25 (mix), danger=No

# Step 2: Add ash if noise detected
if noise > 0.3 then theta pi/3  # Adjust mixture (60 degrees)
step
state  # Expected: R=0.85

# Final state: Durable stone bond achieved (fitness > 0.8)
# Chemical process: 
#   CaO (quicklime) + H2O → Ca(OH)2 (slaked lime/hydration)
#   Ca(OH)2 + CO2 → CaCO3 (limestone/carbonation)
# Ancient recipe: Nile silt + burnt lime for pyramid blocks
# Fitness: f = R*(1-D)*(1-N)*eq
